- op: update  # c5aa
  at: '2026-05-17T20:41:15Z'  # c5aa
  by: agent  # c5aa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c5aa
  clock: 5  # c5aa
  nonce: c5aa  # c5aa
  set:  # c5aa
    title: "Add forward-reference comment from framework_patterns.py to _AUTOLOAD_BY_CONVENTION_FRAMEWORKS docstring (WI-lohok follow-up, downscoped from refactor)"  # c5aa
    description: "**REVISED 2026-05-17 — downscoped from refactor to docs-only after empirical investigation.**\n\n## Original framing (filed 2026-04-26, now superseded)\n\nThe original WI proposed refactoring `_AUTOLOAD_BY_CONVENTION_FRAMEWORKS` at `profile.py:369` from a hardcoded frozenset (currently `{\"rails\"}`) to a data-driven configuration. The motivation was an anticipated need: \"other frameworks may fit the same pattern but the discovery / addition path is unclear.\" Three options were proposed: (a) separate YAML, (b) `autoloaded: true` field in each framework's existing pattern YAML, (c) docstring-only with criteria.\n\n## What the 2026-05-17 investigation found\n\nThe anticipated need did not materialise. Of the candidates the original description flagged — Phoenix, Express, Hanami, Spring Boot, Django, plus other Ruby web frameworks — **none actually need the autoload exemption.** Traced each through the relevant analyzer:\n\n| Framework | Mechanism | Produces import edges? | Needs exemption? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Phoenix (Elixir) | `use Phoenix.LiveView`, `use Phoenix.Controller` | YES (`elixir.py:882-897` emits `edge_type=\"imports\"` / `evidence_type=\"use_directive\"` / `confidence=0.95`) | No |\n| Sinatra, Hanami, Grape, Padrino, Roda (Ruby) | explicit `require 'X'` in app code | YES | No |\n| Express, NestJS, Koa, Fastify (Node.js) | `require()` or ES `import` | YES | No |\n| Django, FastAPI, Flask (Python) | `from X import Y` | YES | No |\n| Spring Boot (Java) | per profile.py path, Java has no import edges and uses a different fallback | N/A — doesn't touch this code | No |\n| Laravel, Symfony, Yii (PHP) | `use Vendor\\Class;` | YES | No |\n\n**Rails is structurally unique.** Bundler's `gem 'rails'` declaration without a corresponding code-level `require 'rails'` is a Ruby idiom that's idiosyncratically convention-heavy. The hardcoded set has been `{\"rails\"}` since the original PR #3388 (2026-04-26, ~21 days at time of investigation), and there is no near-term realistic second entry.\n\n## The actual residual gap (small)\n\nThe 14-line docstring at `profile.py:355-368` is substantial and **already contains the inclusion criteria** plus explicit counter-examples (Sinatra, Django). The criteria question option (c) was meant to address has effectively been answered all along.\n\nWhat's NOT addressed: a YAML author adding a new file to `frameworks/*.yaml` doesn't have a natural breadcrumb pointing them at the autoload docstring. The discoverability path goes through `framework_patterns.py` (the YAML loader), not through `profile.py`, so the criteria docstring is invisible to someone working in the YAML directory.\n\n## Scope (this WI, downscoped)\n\nAdd a 2-3 line forward-reference comment to `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/framework_patterns.py` (top-of-module or near the YAML loader) that says something like:\n\n```python\n# If your framework's canonical usage is manifest-declared but never\n# imported in app code (Rails-style autoload-by-convention), also add\n# its framework ID to `profile._AUTOLOAD_BY_CONVENTION_FRAMEWORKS`.\n# See profile.py:355 docstring for inclusion criteria and counter-examples.\n```\n\nEstimated effort: 5 minutes. No tests needed (comment-only). No coverage impact.\n\n## What this WI is NOT doing (after downscope)\n\n- NOT refactoring the frozenset to a data-driven configuration (premature; no second candidate exists).\n- NOT adding `autoloaded` fields to framework YAMLs (premature; would be `false` for every framework except Rails).\n- NOT modifying `profile.py:369`'s frozenset or its docstring (the docstring is already adequate).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Same as before: actually adding new frameworks to the set (would require empirical evidence of demotion on a real codebase).\n- Loose connection to `INV-vunaf` (framework detection FPs from manifest substring matching) remains a separate axis — see 2026-05-17 discussion entry.\n\n## Closure criterion\n\nThe forward-reference comment lands in `framework_patterns.py` with a pointer to `profile.py:355`'s docstring. Item closes `done`.\n\n## History\n\nOriginal 2026-04-26 framing assumed multiple autoload candidates would surface organically. As of 2026-05-17 investigation, none have. The refactor's premise was anticipatory and the anticipation didn't materialise. Downscoped per maintainer direction to address only the discoverability gap, which is real but small."  # c5aa
  remove:  # c5aa
    tags: [someday]  # c5aa
